course: dictionary
lesson: 2539
title: Defeat: winning, losing and giving up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Defeat is a word you will meet in sport, in stories and in history. As a verb, to defeat someone means to win against them in a game, fight, war or vote. «We defeated the visiting team» means our team won.
explain: As a noun, a defeat is a loss, when you do not win. In «a 3–0 defeat», the score shows the team lost 3 goals to 0. The score is the clue, so defeat must mean a loss.
explain: Sometimes defeat is not about a match at all. «The last question defeated me» means I could not solve it. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: To defeat someone means to win against them.
fact: A defeat is a loss, when you do not win a game, fight or vote.
fact: To admit defeat means to give up.
fact: «Suffer a defeat» means to lose.
fact: «Defeating the purpose» means something stops working or does not succeed.
exercise: «We defeated the visiting team.» What does defeated mean? | *Won against them | Lost to them | Played them at home | Watched them play
exercise: «The score was a 3–0 defeat.» What is a defeat here? | A big party after the match | A new kind of game | A draw with no winner | *A loss, when you do not win
exercise: Which phrase means to give up? | A narrow defeat | Defeat the purpose | Suffer a defeat in the rain | *Admit defeat
test: «The last question defeated me.» What does defeated mean here? | I read it twice | I answered it first | *I could not solve it | I skipped it on purpose
test: In a points table, what does a team's record count? | Shirt colours | Goals scored only | Players' ages | *Wins, draws and defeats
exam: Which sentence uses defeat to mean that something stops working? | «We defeated the other team in the final.» | «He suffered a defeat in the match.» | *«Leaving the lamp on all night defeats the purpose of saving energy.» | «The hero defeated the villain.»
